(Chapter One: Plant Biology) Tj T*
(Plants manufacture their own food through a process that captures) Tj T*
(sunlight. Chlorophyll in the chloroplasts absorbs photons and drives) Tj T*
(the conversion of carbon dioxide and water into glucose and oxygen.) Tj T*
(The light dependent reactions occur in the thylakoid membrane, while) Tj T*
(the Calvin cycle fixes carbon in the stroma. A single leaf can host) Tj T*
(roughly five hundred thousand chloroplasts per square millimetre.) Tj T*
