(Chapter Three: Algorithms) Tj T*
(Binary search locates a value in a sorted array by repeatedly halving) Tj T*
(the interval under consideration. Because the search space shrinks by) Tj T*
(half on every comparison, the running time is logarithmic. An array of) Tj T*
(one million elements needs at most twenty comparisons. The array must) Tj T*
(already be sorted, which is the precondition people most often forget.) Tj T*
ET
